@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# Security audit and deployment
+
+The audit covered every application file. The original HTML had an inline stylesheet
+and one style attribute, no scripts, no dynamic DOM sinks, no messaging, no iframes,
+no popup integrations, and no browser feature requirements. Its only third-party
+request was a CSS background image from images.unsplash.com. The original server
+returned HTML for every path, supplied no security headers, and returned a logout
+message without removing credentials.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `npm start` runs a dependency-free Node HTTP server. An exact route/asset map serves
+  the existing pages and the extracted CSS; source files and unknown paths return 404.
+  Existing navigation destinations continue to show the landing page as before.
+- HTML has no inline styles, scripts, event handlers, or HTML injection sinks.
+  No client-side JavaScript is needed, so CSP disables all scripts. Trusted Types
+  enforcement also blocks DOM injection sinks and policy creation in supporting browsers.
+  Browsers without Trusted Types retain CSP protection.
+- CSP denies resources by default, permits only first-party CSS and the existing
+  Unsplash image origin, forbids framing/base tags/plugins, and restricts forms to
+  this origin. No unsafe-inline, unsafe-eval, wildcard or script-origin exceptions.
+- All responses have no-store caching, nosniff, frame denial, conservative COOP,
+  same-origin CORP, referrer protection, unused-feature restrictions, and Fetch
+  Metadata isolation. Cross-site document links work; subresource requests and
+  mutations from other sites are rejected. Missing metadata is tolerated for older
+  clients; logout additionally requires an exact Origin match.
+- Logout in the navigation uses POST. GET/HEAD `/logout` (and `/logout/`) only offer
+  confirmation, preventing link prefetch or foreign links from signing someone out.
+  Same-origin POST returns a signed-out page, expires received root-path cookies
+  plus `session`/`__Host-session`, and sends `Clear-Site-Data` for cookies, storage,
+  and cache. No visitor input is interpolated into HTML or redirects.
+
+## Deploy
+
+Use a supported Node LTS release. No dependencies or compilation are required.
+Set `NODE_ENV=production`, `PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://your-actual-host.example`, and `PORT`
+(default 11222), then run `npm start` behind an HTTPS reverse proxy. PUBLIC_ORIGIN
+must match the browser's origin exactly (including nondefault ports). The server
+never trusts Host or forwarded headers for security decisions. Block direct public
+access to the backend and preserve response headers through the proxy/CDN.
+
+HTTPS is required for browser Clear-Site-Data support. Explicit cookie expiration
+provides a fallback for root-path, host-only cookies; it cannot remove arbitrary
+Domain/Path cookies. Clear-Site-Data cookies may also affect sibling subdomains;
+use a dedicated site/domain when other applications must retain their cookies.
+This repository has no authentication provider, session store, or login issuance.
+If those are added, revoke the server-side session before returning logout success,
+and use Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Path=/, host-only `__Host-session` cookies.
+Clearing the browser does not invalidate a stolen or copied session token.
+
+HTTPS deployments start with HSTS max-age=300; increase only after confirming the
+HTTPS deployment works. Subdomain inclusion and preload are deliberately omitted.
+Full cross-origin isolation (COEP) is unnecessary here and could block the image.
+There are no external scripts/styles to pin with SRI and no CORS grants.
+
+## Policy rollout and telemetry
+
+The audited, script-free site defaults to `SECURITY_POLICY_MODE=enforce`.
+For future integrations, set `SECURITY_POLICY_MODE=report-only` in staging or during
+a controlled rollout: the full policy is reported while framing, base-tag, plugin,
+and form restrictions remain enforced. Capture real traffic over days/weeks and
+triage violations before restoring `enforce`. A nonce/hash policy is needed before
+adding scripts; do not relax to unsafe-inline or invent a pass-through Trusted Types
+policy. Keep the report endpoints enabled after enforcement.
+
+Reporting-Endpoints points to the configured absolute PUBLIC_ORIGIN plus
+`/security-reports`; CSP uses report-to and legacy report-uri. Browsers may not
+send reports on HTTP. The bounded POST collector accepts modern batches and legacy
+CSP JSON, validates size/type, and logs only allowlisted directive names and counts.
+It discards URLs, query strings, script samples, identifiers, and raw report bodies.
+Configure the proxy/APM not to log report request bodies or URL query strings; apply
+edge rate limits to this unauthenticated endpoint. Reports are untrusted and
+incomplete: extension noise and spoofed reports are not evidence of an attack.
+
+## Verification
+
+`npm run build` checks server/handler syntax without starting or importing the
+server entrypoint. `npm test` contains offline request-handler tests for logout,
+CSRF, headers, report-only mode, report privacy/limits, route isolation, and markup.
+The tests use in-memory streams, never a network listener. Tests and browser checks
+were not executed during this change, in accordance with the build-only constraint.
